{"id":"word:hebrew:H3198","type":"word","title":"יָכַח","subtitle":"H3198 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to be right (i.e. correct); reciprocal, to argue ; causatively, to decide , justify or convict","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to יָכַח (H3198) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 59 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"יָכַח (yâkach) means to be right (i.e. correct); reciprocal, to argue ; causatively, to decide , justify or convict First listed occurrence: 1Chr 12 18."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"יָכַח","transliteration":"yâkach","pronunciation":"yaw-kahh'","strong":"H3198","lemmaId":"hebrew:H3198","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["מוֹכִ֑יחַ","הוֹכֵ֣חַ","וַ/יּ֥וֹכַח","וְ/הוֹכִ֨יחַ֙","וְ/הוֹכִ֥יחַ"],"morphs":[["HVhrmsa",7],["HVhi3ms",6],["HC/Vhq3ms",5],["HVha",5],["HC/Vhw3ms",3],["HC/Vhi3ms",2],["HVhi2ms/Sp1cs",2],["HVhi1cs/Sp2ms",2],["HC/Vhq1cs/Sp3ms",1],["HC/VNrfsa",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"to be right (i.e. correct); reciprocal, to argue ; causatively, to decide , justify or convict","usage":"appoint, argue, chasten, convince, correct(-ion), daysman, dispute, judge, maintain, plead, reason (together), rebuke, reprove(-r), surely, in any wise.","full":"H3198. yakach [ יָכַח ] verb Hiph`il decide, adjudge, prove , (Late Hebrew Pi`el וִכַּח argue with ( עם ), compare Hithpa`el, Hiph`il prove, correct ; Aramaic Pa וַכַּח Aph`el אוֺכַח , id. ) — Hiph`il Perfect הוֺכִיחַ Isa 2:4-5 t.; הֹכִיחַ Gen 24:44 ; הוֺכִחַ 21:25 ; 2 masculine singular חֹכַחְתָּ 24:14 ; 1 singular suffix הוֺכַחְתִּיו 2Sam 7:14 ; Imperfect יוֺכִיחַ Isa 11:3 5 t.; יוֺכַח Hosea 4:4 4 t.; יוֺכָ֑ח 1Chr 12:17 ; suffix יוֺכִיחֵנִי Psa 141:5 12t. Imperfect; Imperative הוֺכַח Prov 9:8 ; Infinitive absolute הוֺכֵחַ Lev 19:17 5 t.; construct הוֺכִיחַ Hab 1:12 ; הַלְהוֺכַח Job 6:26 ; Participle מוֺכִיחַ Ezek 3:26 8 t.; plural מוֺכִיחִים Prov 24:25 ; &#8212; 1 decide, judge , absolute Gen 31:42 (E), 1Chr 12:17 ; Isa 11:3 ; Psa 94:10 ; with לְ decide for Isa 2:4 = Micah 4:3 ; Isa 11:4 ; with בּין , Gen 31:37 (E), Job 9:33 ; אֱלוֺהַּ עִם לְגֶבֶר 16:21 . 2 adjudge, appoint , with לְ , Gen 24:14 , 44 (J). 3 shew to be right, prove , with accusative of thing and על person against Job 19:5 ; with אל person unto 13:15 ; so argue before 13:3 , and (absolute) 15:3 . 4 convince, convict , with accusative of person Psa 50:21 בּ person Prov 30:6 ; with לְ person Job 32:12 . 5 reprove, chide: a. of God , with accusative of person Job 22:4 ; Psa 50:8 ; 105:14 = 1Chr 16:21 ; with בּ object 2Kin 19:4 = Isa 37:4 . b. of man, absolute Hosea 4:4 ; Ezek 3:26 ; Job 6:25 (twice in verse); Prov 24:25 ; 25:12 ; בַּשַּׁעַר מוֺכִיחַ Amos 5:10 ; Isa 29:21 ; with accusative of person Gen 21:25 (E), Lev 19:17 (twice in verse) (H), Prov 9:8 ; 28:23 ; Jer 2:19 ; אֱלוהַּ מוֺכִיחַ Job 40:2 ; accusative of thing 6:26 ; with לְ , Prov 9:7-8 , 15:12 ; 19:25 . 6 correct, rebuke , of God, absolute Hab 1:12 ; with accusative of person Psa 141:5 ; Job 13:10 (twice in verse); בְּשֵׁבֶט 2Sam 7:14 ; happy the man whom God corrects Job 5:17 ; for God loves him Prov 3:12 ; God is entreated not to correct in anger Psa 6:2 ; 38:2 . Hoph`al Perfect בְּמַכְאוֺב וְהוּכַח he is chastened also with pain Job 33:19 . Niph`al Imperfect וְנִוָָּֽכְחָה לְכוּנָֿא Isa 1:18 come now and let us reason together; Participle עִמּוֺ נוֺכָח יָשָׁר שָׁם Job 23:7 there an upright man might reason with him ; feminine (passive) וְנֹכָ֑חַת Gen 20:16 (E), but Di SS read וְנֹכַחַתְּ 2feminine singular Perfect and thou art set right, righted, justified. Hithpa`el Imperfect יִתְוַכָּח עִםוִֿשְׂרָאֵל Micah 6:2 with Israel he will argue (|| לי ׳רִיב עִם ).","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 12 18","keyReferences":["1Chr 12 18","1Chr 16 21","2Kgs 19 4","2Sam 7 14","Amos 5 10","Ezek 3 26"